      "values": []
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "458004c2-2f2b-40bf-8fd7-cad968995e49",
      "key": "3f0876dc-3dc1-49ac-b396-b7b217a40b09",
      "values": []
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "34e5aa3b-db10-40a1-893d-79e98cd3f2f4",
      "key": "fff940ee-7da2-4ee7-a7d9-a522c0c781cd",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "featurePropertyFeatureTitle",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Features"
        },
        {
          "alias": "richTextContent",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cul\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003EHalf board accommodation\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003EAll excursions \u0026amp; guided tours included\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003EBlue Badge guide Days 3 to 4\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003EExecutive coach throughout\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003EOne free place per 10 paying passengers\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003C/ul\u003E\n"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "1d09b5af-b95a-4af5-b8f2-323db029e817",
      "key": "cf43faab-197c-4926-b63f-4c56dd275d8d",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "featurePropertyFeatureTitle",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Accommodation"
        },
        {
          "alias": "richTextContent",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EFour nights on half board basis at the 3* White Swan Hotel at Alnwick. Ideally situated to visit the sights and attractions this itinerary has to offer, facilities at the hotel include a restaurant and a bar and all rooms are en suite.\u003C/p\u003E\n"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "2d9b0603-29ef-423a-8d3e-d9c039d3d7b1",
      "key": "2f5f0e88-d161-400d-adeb-11738fa1b6b4",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "featurePropertyFeatureTitle",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Sights"
        },
        {
          "alias": "richTextContent",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cul\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003EDurham Cathedral - guided tour\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003EMellerstain House - guided tour\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003EPaxton House\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003EAlnwick Castle\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003ECragside House \u0026amp; Gardens\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003ELindisfarne Castle\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003EBamburgh Castle\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003EChillingham Castle\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003C/ul\u003E\n"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "de535189-b468-4594-8118-f303bac50e3c",
      "key": "48f228c9-d3a2-4709-b778-a96fe8faf6cf",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "featurePropertyFeatureTitle",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Tailor your sights"
        },
        {
          "alias": "richTextContent",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cul\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003EFord and Etal Estate - home to the Joicey family for over 100 years, the estate is centred on the villages of Ford and Etal in the valley of the River Till between the Scottish Borders and the Cheviot Hills and a guided tour takes in Lady Waterford Hall, commissioned in 1860 by Louisa Anne, Marchioness of Waterford, and the 14th century Etal Castle\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003ETraquair House - dating back to 1107, it is said to be the oldest inhabited house in Scotland and a guided tour reveals its colourful historical associations such as the Jacobite Risings and visits by 27 monarchs, including Mary Queen of Scots\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003EBrinkburn Priory - the English Heritage 12th century church of the Augustinian priory of Brinkburn is picturesquely set by a bend in the River Coquet\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003C/ul\u003E\n"
          }
        },
        {
          "alias": "featurePropertyFeatureDescription",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Here are some more suggested places of interest you might like to include:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "837beecf-4239-4b3d-b683-1d611af3da2e",
      "key": "27233890-9dfe-417b-923b-353f3ba9e17b",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "richTextContent",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Ch3\u003EDay 1 \u2013 Durham Cathedral\u003C/h3\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EBoard our private executive coach at your preferred pick up points \u2013 travel to Durham for a guided tour of the Cathedral, once described as \u2018one of the great architectural experiences of Europe\u2019 and a renowned masterpiece of Romanesque architecture \u2013 check in at the 3* White Swan Hotel at Alnwick.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Ch3\u003EDay 2 \u2013 Mellerstain House \u0026amp; Paxton House\u003C/h3\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EGuided tour of Mellerstain House, an exquisite Robert Adam stately home built between 1725 and 1778, taking in the library which is regarded as one of Robert Adams finest creations and a fine collection of paintings and period furniture \u2013 built for a German princess in 1756 by John and James Adam, Paxton House is one of the finest Palladian houses in Britain containing the preeminent Scottish collection of Chippendale furniture and acting as an outstation of the National Galleries of Scotland.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Ch3\u003EDay 3 \u2013 Alnwick Castle \u0026amp; Cragside House and Gardens\u003C/h3\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EOur Blue Badge guide accompanies us to Alnwick Castle, the second largest inhabited castle in England, the first being Windsor Castle, and home of the Percys, Earls and Dukes of Northumberland since 1309 \u2013 described as \u2018the palace of a modern magician\u2019, the National Trust\u2019s Cragside House and Gardens is a wonderful Victorian mansion dating from the 19th century whose interior features state of the art hydraulics powering a revolutionary lift system and internal telephones which mesmerised visitors in its time.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Ch3\u003EDay 4 \u2013 Lindisfarne Castle \u0026amp; Bamburgh Castle\u003C/h3\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EThe National Trust\u2019s Lindisfarne Castle on Holy Island is a romantic 16th century castle with spectacular views that was transformed by Lutyens into an Edwardian holiday home \u2013 Bamburgh Castle overlooking the Farne Islands was once home to the kings of ancient Northumbria and is now home to a fine collection of armour, porcelain, furniture and art.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Ch3\u003EDay 5 \u2013 Chillingham Castle\u003C/h3\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EThe 12th century Chillingham Castle in Alnwick was King Edward I\u2019s base camp for the 1298 conquering attack on William Wallace and our guided tour takes in the \u2018Long Galleries\u2019 added by the Elizabethans and the Italian garden laid out in the 19th century by Sir Jeffrey Wyatville \u2013 return to our original departure points with comfort stops en route.\u003C/p\u003E\n"
          }
        },
        {
          "alias": "featurePropertyFeatureTitle",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Suggested Itinerary"
        },
        {
          "alias": "featurePropertyFeatureDescription",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Every one of our tours is exclusively for your group and your group alone so each one can be tailor made to suit the interests and profile of your members until you have a tour with an itinerary and at a price which matches the interests and profile of your members."
        },
        {
          "alias": "featurePropertyFeatureSummary",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "Remember this itinerary is just our suggestion. "
          }
        }
      ]
    },
